<title>UK: UK Sept net consumer credit up s/a 1.067 bln stg.</title>
<headline>UK Sept net consumer credit up s/a 1.067 bln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England released the following seasonally-adjusted consumer credit data -</p>
<p>NET LENDING (previously released data in brackets, in MLN stg)</p>
<p>					 Sept	Aug	     Sept 95</p>
<p> Total net lending		2,420     2,629(2,673)   1,976</p>
<p> -- Consumer credit	     1,067     1,044 (997)	609</p>
<p> -- On dwellings		  1,353     1,585 (1,676)  1,367</p>
<p>BREAKDOWN OF NET CONSUMER LENDING BY SOURCE</p>
<p> -- Banks			     890	 607   (578)    491</p>
<p> -- Building Soc		    32	  22    (24)	21</p>
<p> -- Other specialist lenders    137	 409  (407)     104</p>
<p> -- Retailers			 12	  12   (-3)	-4</p>
<p> -- Insurance co		    -4	  -6   (-9)	-3</p>
<p> -- Credit card		    149	 314  (326)     232</p>
<p>CONSUMER CREDIT (seasonally adjusted in pct)</p>
<p> Consumer credit mth/mth	     1.5	 1.5  (1.4)     1.0</p>
<p>		     3mth annualised   20.2	17.7 (17.1)    12.4</p>
<p>		     6mth annualised   18.1	17.1 (16.8)    12.1</p>
<p>		     year-on-year	16.2	15.6 (15.5)    12.7</p>
<p> Total Personal borrowing mth/mth  0.5	 0.6  (0.6)     0.4</p>
<p>		     3mth annualised   6.7	 6.5  (6.5)     4.9</p>
<p>		     6mth annualised   6.4	 6.3  (6.3)     5.0</p>
<p>		     year-on-year	5.9	 5.8  (5.9)     5.5</p>
<p> Secured on Dwellings mth/mth	0.3	 0.4  (0.4)     0.4</p>
<p>		     3mth annualised   4.5	 4.6  (4.8)     3.7</p>
<p>		     6mth annualised   4.5	 4.5  (4.6)     3.9</p>
<p>		     year-on-year	4.3	 4.3  (4.3)     4.4</p>
<p>Note - Consensus forecast was for an 830 million stg rise in net credit.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
